**Two latent data-layer bugs found + fixed during Step 7 integration:**
- `mock-seed.spec.ts` imported `opportunityDetailFromRow` without exporting it (spec failed to compile).
- `opportunityDetailFromRow` hardcoded `risk_level: 'MEDIUM'` instead of reading `financials.risk_level`.

**Full suite: 956/956 vitest green + 9/9 payouts e2e green (byte-identical render).**

## How It Was Built (orchestrator workflow)

- cline-one job 5 (payouts rewire) TIMED OUT at 600s (exit 124) while
  *planning* the spec edits — the page file was fully rewired but the spec
  + data-file deletion were left undone. Orchestrator finished the spec,
  deleted `payouts.data.ts`, and ran the e2e gate.
- The e2e gate surfaced `NG2003` (ApiTransport is a type-only interface,
  unusable as an Angular DI token) — closed via the `API_TRANSPORT`
  InjectionToken. This gap was invisible to the unit specs because they
  construct `new ApiClient(transport)` directly (bypassing DI).
- Lesson: a passing unit suite over manually-constructed collaborators does
  NOT prove the DI graph wires up in a real app — the e2e/ng-serve gate is
  what catches it. See decision log 2026-08-18.

